      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-4786: the fix for CVE-2026-4519 could be bypassed in webbrowser.open() through %action substitution, so a URL could still inject options or commands for some browsers. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/148169 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/a4d3edf3a6ecfde504d02126410d2a65a859b744), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-4786. Checked Lib/webbrowser.py for the dash check applied after %action substitution (self._check_url(url.replace(\"%action\", action))) in the python-3.12 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.16-r4, x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. Builds before 3.12.13-r4 lack the fix; 3.12.13-r4 and every later build have it. The range ends at 3.12.13-r4."
